        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(control-ui): import Codex and Claude Code memory",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw operators can migrate coding-assistant configuration from the CLI, but the Control UI had no reviewed way to discover and import Codex consolidated memory or Claude Code auto-memory into a selected agent workspace.\n\nCloses #106215\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds additive `migrations.memory.plan` and `migrations.memory.apply` Gateway methods plus provider-owned Codex and Claude Code memory discovery. Plans are agent-scoped, memory-only, fingerprinted, and rebuilt before apply. Exact item selection, workspace-bounded no-follow writes, no-clobber replacement staging, verified pre-import backups, item backups, reports, and recovery metadata keep the web flow reviewable and recoverable.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSettings now includes **Import Memory**. Operators can select an agent, preview Codex and Claude Code memory collections without exposing file contents to the browser, choose exact files, import them, and explicitly replace existing imports after a refreshed conflict preview. Imported files live under the selected workspace's `memory/imports/` tree; source memory remains unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live Control UI proof on macOS with real local Codex and Claude Code memory: imported 2 Codex files and a selective 4-file Claude collection, refreshed conflicts, exercised replacement, verified the pre-import archive plus item backups, and byte-compared Codex source/destination files.\n- Behavior-validator black-box contract: 5 passed, 0 failed, 0 blocked.\n- Remote focused suite: 159 tests passed across 8 Vitest shards, including Gateway protocol/handlers, provider discovery/apply, selection, fs-safe writes, navigation, and the new page (`https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29252085729`).\n- Remote `pnpm check:changed`: passed all generated-surface, typecheck, lint, security, database-first, and architecture guards.\n- Remote `pnpm build`: passed core/package build, plugin SDK export verification, Control UI production build, precompressed asset verification, and UI performance budgets.\n- Autoreview: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
